module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.witness_module_absent_from_the_executed_set

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data witness_module_absent_from_the_executed_set: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "witness_module_absent_from_the_executed_set" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a witness module that discriminates correctly is absent from the runner's executed set** (THE CHECK IS RIGHT, ITS ARMS ARE ENROLLED, AND ITS SUBJECT IS REAL -- the only missing thing is membership in the population the required run actually schedules, so every signal a reader consults says covered and none of them is the one that decides.",

    "THE INVALID STATE is a claim module present on disk, correct, and named in no schedule the required lane reads. The harm is that a green verdict is cited as coverage for the class that module owns. A floor verdict names what it EXECUTED; it cannot name what it never saw, and the reader supplies the missing quantifier without noticing.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: 2 on paper and BELOW THE LADDER in fact. The mechanism exists and would fire; DESIGN.md section 4b(2) makes rung 2 conditional on that mechanism EXECUTING and STAYING ENROLLED, so an unenrolled wall holds no rung at all. This is the inert-lens tier the design document names: the machinery exists and nothing gates on it.",

    "SPECIMEN, gunbc#10688. Three hand-authored consumers still read `item_registry` by bare leaf after the registry was re-keyed on declaration identity, so the whole-graph read missed every time and every row silently took the unexpanded local entry. `test.claim.resolved_rust_fn_service_chain_consumer_witness` CATCHES THIS -- rebuilding with the fix reverted turns its shallow arm red -- and it was green across the whole branch, because the module appears nowhere in `src/v2/workflow/` and therefore never enters the executed set. `verdict=FloorClean` over 3551 claims was silent about it, and a cross-module claim added in the same PR inherited the dormancy: `planned` stayed 3551.",

    "THE DISTINGUISHING FACT, and the reason this is its own row rather than an instance of a narrow-subject check: THE WITNESS AND THE CLASS ARE BOTH PRESENT AND CORRECT. Nothing about the check is wrong. A reader who opens the file finds discriminating arms, a red control and an accurate name; a reader who greps the corpus finds the class covered; a reader who reads the floor verdict finds it clean. The defect is a JOIN that nobody performs -- claim modules on disk against claim modules scheduled -- and it is invisible from either side alone. Compare [[discriminating_arm_built_but_never_enrolled]], where the file itself withholds the arm, and [[a_written_row_is_not_a_firing_mechanism]].",

    "THE CHEAP DETECTOR is a set difference the runner could compute for free: claim modules discovered on disk MINUS claim modules the required lanes schedule, printed with the verdict. Any non-empty remainder is a population the green does not speak for. The floor already prints `outside_this_runs_universe`, so the shape exists; what is missing is that a module absent from every schedule never reaches that accounting at all -- it is outside the universe of the thing that reports being outside the universe.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: before citing a green run as coverage for a class, ask which SCHEDULE named the claim, not which file declares it. A claim's existence and a claim's execution are two facts, and only the second is what a verdict reports.",

    "FOURTH INDEPENDENT INSTANCE OF ONE SHAPE IN A SINGLE NIGHT, which is the argument that this is a class and not a coincidence: a check whose FORM is right and whose POPULATION is narrower than its name implies. The others, found by three other lanes: regen asking the filesystem a question `seed_retention_frontier` owns; doc_reachability asserting duplicate-key rather than slug-to-file; heal reporting SUCCESS on a head where build was red, because heal does not install that population. Each was individually reasonable and none was written down as a population claim, which is exactly why four of them could stand at once.)",

    "THE SAME ABSENCE HIDES REDS, NOT ONLY FALSE GREENS, and that is a second harm this row did not state. Every instance above is a CORRECT check whose green is cited as coverage; the absence is dangerous because nobody learns the class is unchecked. But a module outside the executed set is also free to BREAK and stay broken: nothing reports it, so the file rots in place while reading as ordinary committed evidence. gunbc#11025, 2026-09-11: three witnesses in `v2.test.claim.long.accumulator_copy_compile_gate` failed at evaluation with `no field 'kind' on type 'NormalizedTree'` -- a real defect, loud when run -- and had been failing for an unknown length of time. The entry is a `LegacyFrozenPathDeferral` in `gunbc.witness.witness_deferral_freeze`, admitted by PATH POLICY with no executing consumer, so all four of its witnesses execute nowhere in any required lane and three of them could sit red indefinitely. The repair was one field; the reason it survived was membership.",

    "SO THE ADMISSION MECHANISM MATTERS, AND IT IS NOT ALWAYS AN OMISSION. The instances above are modules nobody scheduled -- a gap. This one was scheduled OUT, deliberately, by a path-policy rule that admits an entry as deferred: the roster that records it is itself the evidence, and it is honest about what it is. The class is the same because the consequence is identical (no executing consumer), but the DETECTION differs: a gap is found by joining modules-on-disk to modules-scheduled, while a deferral is already written down and needs only to be read as what it says. A deferral roster is therefore a list of modules whose reds nobody will see, and it can be consulted directly rather than derived.",

    "SPECIMEN, 2026-10-07, the same absence HIDING A STANDING RED, and the strongest form of the second harm. test.claim.self_host_emitted_call_target_realization_witness::w_depth_one_shared_field_refutation_stays_shape_guarded FAILS against main at the IMMUTABLE sha 1728bcc0ab4e7d8285359f161612d4c1226812f2 (Gate parse_acceptance_census: accepted arm on the smallest module, census phase 3, #13415) -- claim_batch claim-run at that sha, exit=1, FAIL=1, BuildBuddy remote dispatch completed 2026-10-07T08:27:47.537Z, discovering session vivid-lynx-377 job j36fc601a, command and output retained in the session transcript -- and every unrepaired descendant of that sha inherits the red. No STANDING gate executed it: the ordinary prepared subject excludes modules outside the required-gate closure, and changed-witness selection replaces that disposition only when a diff selects the identity -- which is exactly how the red surfaced: an unrelated PR touched the entry's sibling probes, inherited three defunct-import reds from the #13388 re-homing, and ran the whole set. The failing witness synthesizes a std-types-only probe (a shared coproduct matched at depth one inside a record pattern) and imports neither v2.std.optional nor any renamed spelling; the red predates every edit on the discovering branch. THE HONEST CEILING IS RUNG 2: a red witness on main stays writable -- a scheduled full-corpus lane would only expose and block it -- so rung 3 is not on offer. THE HONEST NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER is that lane IMPLEMENTED AND ENROLLED, not a sign-off: a standing claim run over a DEFINED CLAIM-ROOT POPULATION that refuses, or invokes a declared remedy, on every red or non-verdict, DEMONSTRATED FAILING on a planted or standing red. Manual attribution -- running the entry on main's own tree before blaming the discovering PR -- is how this specimen was found, and it is a discipline, not a rung.",

    "POPULATION FORM OF THE SAME JOIN FAILURE, and the specimen that generalises it. Measured 2026-10-19 at origin/main 45fdd50224891a6414e00ddd01132493e1113233 by the CHEAP DETECTOR query above: SEVEN modules declare test fn bodies, sit inside a witness_layer_roots layer (dag, src/v2), are named by no execution roster, and fall outside all three witness_discovery_scan_dirs -- 67 test fn bodies in total, every one of them a real discriminating assertion that CI never executes. The population, bodies first: 17 src/v2/workflow/orchestration_retry_emit.dag, 16 src/v2/workflow/orchestration_emit.dag, 12 src/v2/workflow/orchestration_bash.dag, 8 src/v2/workflow/orchestration_tier2_emit.dag, 8 src/v2/lens/mandatory_tag/corpus_scan_witness.dag, 4 src/v2/workflow/orchestration_while_emit.dag, 2 src/v2/lens/no_dual_representation.dag (per-file list corrected 2026-10-21 against the detector query above, which at 45fdd5022489 prints 4 for orchestration_while_emit and 2 for no_dual_representation; the earlier transcription read 8 and named src/v2/lens/realization_vocabulary_containment.dag, which the query does not return; the 67 total was right and is unmoved). Each compiles at 0 blocking error(s) with ZERO test fn reaching the runner, so every signal a reader consults -- the file compiles, it has tests, the floor is clean -- says covered, and the only signal that decides (presence in the executed set) is the one nobody reads.",

    "HOW THIS SPECIMEN WAS FOUND, which is the point. It was not looked for: it surfaced while reading src/v2/workflow/orchestration_while_emit.dag at 0dc3f0ab4c1fe112c13b10d6cbc991a94f3744fd to decide whether a deletion was safe, and deleting the production route through that file's one bracket operator turned NOTHING red anywhere -- compiles stayed at 0 blocking error(s) and no witness count moved. Ceiling, stated so the row does not talk itself out of the check it asks for: the condition is mechanically preventable, so an enrolled coherence witness over it sits at RUNG 2, not rung 3 -- a module in a witness_layer_roots layer that declares test fn bodies, lies outside every witness_discovery_scan_dirs entry and is named by no execution roster is decidable from the Node tree plus gunbc.ci.ci_layer_roots. It is absent because it changes what CI executes and pays for, which is an operator call wider than a ledger row -- not because the fact is unreadable. gunbc.ci.ci_layer_roots already distinguishes deliberately-non-executing namespaces (non_executing_witness_module_prefixes = \"v1\"), so 'unrun on purpose' versus 'unrun by accident' is expressible in the authority and simply unenforced for the layer roots.",

    "COUNTING DISCIPLINE THIS ROW OWES, because the naive figure is wrong and was nearly used. Dropping only the */test/* filter (a path filter, NOT the scan-dir filter) turns 7 modules and 67 bodies into 888 modules and 6320 bodies, because dag/ and src/v2/ are full of ordinary claim modules; the 7/67 figure survives precisely BECAUSE the scan-dir filter is applied, since every scan dir sits under a test path. Of the 67, 42 are in dag/gunbc/witness/witness_row_cost_basis.tsv; DATA_ROWS=1146 and DISTINCT_RUN_REF=1 are readings of the same file at the same commit. Every number here is a DATED OBSERVATION at the two heads named in this row (origin/main 45fdd5022489 for the population, 0dc3f0ab4c1f for the discovery), re-derivable from the two authority lists, never copied forward as authority.",

    "WHAT THE PORTED COVERAGE IS AND IS NOT, stated so nobody reads it as production safety: the 9 tests PROPOSED in pull request #14489 as test.claim.path_predicate_bash_lowering_witness (including the 3 that pin the dirname ascent and its two POSIX-name guards) -- pending, not merged, absent from main at this head, so nothing here is existing coverage until that pull request lands -- exercise a TYPED SUBSTRATE WITH NO PRODUCTION CALLER. Nothing emitted today passes through bash_path_predicate_target_model or bash_dirname_ascent_target_model: the production line that used them was deleted as a no-consumer chain, and the callers were src/v2/workflow/orchestration_while_emit.dag, which CI never discovers, that witness itself, and ONE non-test caller, src/v2/workflow/ci_floor_peak_emit.dag via the bash_nearest_ancestor_locate_assign_command, bash_nearest_ancestor_locate_cond_command and bash_nearest_ancestor_locate_body_command wrappers; that last caller is itself pull request #14467's deletion subject, so it is not a production route either, but it is not a test, so the chain is called by a live non-test module until #14467 lands. They are coverage of a substrate kept for a hypothetical future typed path-test route, plus a guard against a future emitter shipping d;rm -rf / into an emitted program if that route is ever taken -- NOT evidence that any emitted program is safe today, and they must not be cited as if they were.",

    "ISLAND NAMED AS THE DELETION TRIGGER'S POPULATION -- PROPOSED, NOT BUILT, AND HEADED AS MEASURED. SPECIMEN, AND THE FORWARD REFERENCE IS LABELLED AS ONE: at the head this receipt was written, src/v2/workflow/orchestration_while_emit.dag is still present and the 8-body reading above is a live fact about it. It is NO LONGER PROPOSED: the deletion is BUILT on branch session/zesty-tern-692-pr7, whose own pull request carries this receipt -- the number is a property of the hosting service and is not transcribed here (a reader resolves it from the branch); at the head that lands this sentence the file src/v2/workflow/orchestration_while_emit.dag is absent, and the CHEAP DETECTOR query re-run over the same authority lists at this head returns SIX modules and 63 bodies (17 src/v2/workflow/orchestration_retry_emit, 16 src/v2/workflow/orchestration_emit, 12 src/v2/workflow/orchestration_bash, 8 src/v2/workflow/orchestration_tier2_emit, 8 src/v2/lens/mandatory_tag/corpus_scan_witness, 2 src/v2/lens/no_dual_representation) against SEVEN and 67 at the base head -- exactly the 4 orchestration_while_emit bodies gone, the rest unmoved; the same query at 45fdd5022489 reproduces 7/67, so the total in the POPULATION receipt re-derives while its per-file list does not: the detector prints 4 bodies for src/v2/workflow/orchestration_while_emit.dag and 2 for src/v2/lens/no_dual_representation.dag, not the 8 and the src/v2/lens/realization_vocabulary_containment.dag named there; the list did not match its own query's output, and the POPULATION receipt now carries what the query prints. The 8-body and 67-body readings above are retained as the dated measurements they always claimed to be, at the two heads named; the arm it tested (PipelineStep::While plus orch_emit_while_step in v2.compiler.emit_orchestration) survives deliberately as the declared frontier of gunbc.plans.for_while_loop_sugar. Scope, ENUMERATED BY NAME before any further root is uprooted (§3). At the head this sentence was written, the dirname/cmdsubst-call chain (bash_dirname_ascent_target_model, orch_cmdsubst_assign_call_target_model, orch_call_target_model) and the PathPredicate ladder are NOT dangling: they have exactly one non-test caller, src/v2/workflow/ci_floor_peak_emit.dag, which imports the locate wrappers bash_nearest_ancestor_locate_assign_command, bash_nearest_ancestor_locate_cond_command and bash_nearest_ancestor_locate_body_command (lines 23-25) and calls them (lines 72, 76, 80), and those wrappers call into the chain (bash_orch_if.dag bash_nearest_ancestor_locate_body_command calls bash_dirname_ascent_target_model). So deleting the chain now would uproot a route a non-test module still enters. The chain becomes deletable only AFTER pull request #14467 lands, because that pull request deletes src/v2/workflow/ci_floor_peak_emit.dag itself as its own no-consumer chain; once it has, the census must be RE-RUN at that head, and only if every surviving caller is a test does the chain and the tests that only test it go together -- deleting dead code together with the tests that only test it is NOT the defect this row files, because nothing survives untested. Until #14467 lands, no such deletion is authorised from this row. TRIGGER -- what dissolves this row: an operator CI-policy decision. Either (a) add src/v2/workflow (and the two src/v2/lens files) to witness_discovery_scan_dirs, which makes the assertions execute but pulls in the whole self-witnessed family and its cost; (b) delete the population along with the code it guards; or (c) install the rung-2 coherence witness above so an unrun self-witness refuses at compile time. The decision is outward-facing (it changes what CI executes and pays for) and belongs to the operator, not to whoever notices. Until then the population has no entry point at all, and the missing .dag producer plus its gunbc test label is the follow-up that turns it into an instrument. The kept While arm earns its own falsifier when for_while_loop_sugar gives it a real constructor; until then it is a plan frontier, not coverage.",


  ],

  evidence: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.ci.ci_layer_roots", decl_name: "witness_discovery_scan_dirs"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.ci.ci_layer_roots", decl_name: "witness_layer_roots"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.ci.ci_layer_roots", decl_name: "non_executing_witness_module_prefixes"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "v2.compiler.emit_orchestration", decl_name: "orch_emit_while_step"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "v2.workflow.orchestration_retry_emit", decl_name: "orch_retry_byte_identical_to_hand_authored_holds"),
  ],
}
